  "text": "Hypothesis 3 is the only one the abstract supports.\n\n- **Hypothesis 3** matches the main quantile regression results. The abstract reports that electricity consumption and real GDP increase environmental degradation, and that trade and urbanization reduce EF. It does not mention life expectancy, and the spectral Granger results are a separate finding, so the match is partial, but the core claims agree.\n- **Hypothesis 1** describes a structural equation model with interaction terms involving renewables, human capital, and urbanization. The abstract reports neither that design nor those moderators.\n- **Hypothesis 2** says trade openness increases EF and that human capital mediates the trade and urbanization effects through SEM. The abstract finds trade reduces EF, and reports no mediation analysis.\n- **Hypothesis 4** relies on Bayesian quantile regression with urbanization × R&D interactions. The abstract describes ordinary quantile regression and reports no interaction effects or R&D variable.\n\nCHOICE: 3",
